# Keep diagrams in Markdown in sync > The CI guard
# ipm-overview:docs/use-cases/embed-in-markdown.md#L69
# 32b3cda0b610d6636b3bbd17b9ddce57b43ec80b

# The whole trip: a person pushes, CI guards, the change merges. The GUARD is
# only the middle of it — it contains what CI itself does, and not the push
# (another actor, earlier, elsewhere) nor the merge (after it, once green).
whole::a Take a change through the guard ::e

push::a Push a branch ::e
  --> guard::a Guard the diagrams in CI ::e
  --> merge::a Merge ::e
push, guard, merge --::P--> whole

check::a Check markers and SVGs on push ::e
  --> validate::a Validate the graphs on push ::e
check, validate --::P--> guard

md-embed ::t --> check
ipm-validate ::t --> validate
ciwf::a CI workflow ::t --> check, validate

page::a docs page .md ::t --> check, validate
svg::a committed SVG ::t --> check
user::a User ::t --> push, merge

md-embed ::t --> embedder ::c, command-line tool ::c
ipm-validate ::t --> validator ::c, command-line tool ::c
ciwf --> CI check ::c
page --> Markdown page ::c
svg --> ipm SVG ::c
user --> Maintainer ::c
